  <section class="section soft research-example" id="ded-control">
    <p class="eyebrow">Example research / DED process control</p>
    <h2>
      Adaptive, Productive, and Quality (APQ) control for directed energy
      deposition
    </h2>
    <div class="project-layout project-layout--with-media">
      <div class="project-story">
        <h3>Problem</h3>
        <p>
          DED often relies on preset laser power, machine feed rate, and powder
          flow. Actual deposition can deviate from the intended geometry,
          leaving insufficient material and requiring additional deposition—or
          restarting the build. A key challenge for closed-loop control is
          adjusting powder delivery quickly enough to correct these deviations.
        </p>
        <p>
          Thermal management presents another challenge. The substantial heat
          input creates temperature gradients that can lead to distortion,
          cracking, and residual stresses.
        </p>
        <h3>Approach</h3>
        <p>
          ARMS developed a Dynamic Powder Splitting System (DPSS) that rapidly
          adjusts powder delivery, enabling responsive closed-loop deposition
          control. The broader Adaptive, Productive, and Quality (APQ) framework
          combines monitoring of deposition height, width, and temperature with
          coordinated regulation of energy fluence and powder fluence.
        </p>
        <p>
          To address thermal gradients, the ALP module uses an infrared camera
          to assess the temperature distribution after each deposited layer. The
          controller then automatically reorders the deposition sequence in the
          supplied NC program to reduce temperature gradients.
        </p>
        <h3>Demonstrated result</h3>
        <p>
          The developed control methods improved deposition productivity and
          geometric accuracy, while adaptive sequencing addressed thermal
          gradients during the build.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="project-media-stack">
        <figure class="wide-figure">
          <img
            class="apq-diagram"
            src="/images/apq-control-lossless.webp"
            width="1200"
            height="671"
            loading="lazy"
            alt="APQ control system linking temperature, deposition height, and width measurements to energy and geometry control modules and powder delivery through the DPSS"
          />
          <figcaption>
            APQ DED control architecture, integrating monitoring, energy
            control, and DPSS-based powder delivery.
            <a class="figure-enlarge" href="/images/apq-control-lossless.webp">
